---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Join Us — Wright Lab">
  <main class="page">
    <span class="section-eyebrow">Join Us</span>
    <h1>Open positions and how to apply</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      We welcome motivated trainees and collaborators who want to work at the intersection of
      quantitative proteomics, cell biology, and disease mechanism.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p class="callout-title">The lab is actively recruiting.</p>
      <p>
        This is a ground-floor opportunity to help build a new research program from its earliest
        stage, with room to shape projects, take real ownership, and publish first-author work. We
        are currently looking for graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, and rotation students.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>What we look for</h2>
    <p>
      The lab brings together wet-lab biochemistry, mass-spectrometry proteomics, and computational
      analysis. The strongest applicants are curious about more than one of these areas and are
      eager to learn the others. No single background is required, and we welcome applicants from
      molecular biology, biochemistry, analytical chemistry, and computational backgrounds. What
      matters most is rigor, persistence, and a genuine interest in how signaling complexes govern
      cell fate.
    </p>

    <h2>Graduate students</h2>
    <p>
      Prospective PhD students should apply through the relevant University of Iowa graduate program
      and are encouraged to arrange a laboratory rotation. Students in the lab take ownership of a
      project that spans experimental design, proteomic data generation, and analysis, and are
      supported in presenting at national meetings and publishing first-author work. If you are
      unsure which graduate program is the best fit, email us and we will help you find out.
    </p>

    <h2>Postdoctoral researchers</h2>
    <p>
      We consider postdoctoral applicants who hold a doctoral degree and have a track record in one
      or more of proteomics, mass spectrometry, protein biochemistry, cell biology, or computational
      biology. Postdocs are mentored toward independence, with the goal of building a distinct
      research program and a competitive record for the next career stage. To apply, email a cover
      letter describing your research interests, a CV, and the names of three references.
    </p>

    <h2>Undergraduate and rotation students</h2>
    <p>
      Undergraduates and rotating graduate students are welcome and are paired with a mentor and a
      well-scoped project. Reach out early, since positions are limited by available bench space and
      mentoring capacity.
    </p>

    <h2>Collaborators</h2>
    <p>
      We partner with laboratories that want to apply proximity-labeling proteomics to their own
      systems, and with groups developing complementary methods. If your question involves the
      composition or dynamics of a protein complex in a disease model, we would be glad to talk.
    </p>

    <h2>How to apply</h2>
    <p>
      Email
      <a href="mailto:michael-e-wright@uiowa.edu">michael-e-wright@uiowa.edu</a>
      with a short note about your interests and background, and attach a CV. Full contact details
      are on the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </main>

  <style>
    .callout {
      background: rgba(10, 165, 164, 0.08);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent, #0aa5a4);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
      margin: 1.75rem 0 2.5rem;
    }
    .callout-title {
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--color-text, inherit);
      margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }
    .callout p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  </style>
</Layout>
